{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_010850df770996483730a7a309904276ebe4ec30a63cf802defa27809149e677","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4b5abfdcdc56baf40a7ff034169854048aca1a5e4d9b0a20cd2c9c4b49879162"],"source_ids":["src_6b028023847e540a8896aa333212b8e4"],"text":"Development effort has largely moved to mini-SWE-agent, which the maintainers say matches SWE-agent's performance while being much simpler, and they recommend it going forward.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_05528c43d5e9fee1fe2d4db10c2780d030a926c7594d3d8bda04c111a6def000","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9c53d84ed08d301eddc62dce52d09ef7b99abced1cd737db8d84839ff997d5bd","slc_bda2afac9367a2af8b906ef670f164fa3b725aeb0ea74d059e6af612aa929e6a","slc_cc6b391043f38f19b8af32ba87ce207918282535da20497b514169fdd1a961de"],"source_ids":["src_7da161cf69c45f85bc6607ef9dafe3bd"],"text":"Multimodal support is provided via config/default_mm_with_images.yaml, which enables GitHub issue image processing to base64, an image_tools bundle, a web_browser bundle, and an image_parsing history processor.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_05d8b3693196e5dbdaf446f6b3c2e5d82116af3dc955d3dce027b23578d3dea9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_27389cd2c1cc5718fb3ecba49c1434e105d4157a9cf88f6c6206883821edd12c","slc_68d30575074adb002505ebecaccd16d9904b29b6b9b3af4881e0b94b4627d715"],"source_ids":["src_6b028023847e540a8896aa333212b8e4"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are welcomed via GitHub issues and pull requests, with discussion in issues encouraged before larger code changes; CI badges show pytest, docs builds, codecov, pre-commit, and link checking.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_067eb2c8014a11d047985bcfee103453e823e2032d7943c8f2b8b103657f6cb5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_49ef817434f3f881dbd9a593cc00f383c73df6512c76229a61aa2b7b53184cb1","slc_4e5183ffd5adc44eec1e5580b006a63a2499292af3d555ce2a84908c1b8c1ad1","slc_a836128efa493174bcbc205a501a74ffb6143230e7a0286e1b2a2c81745d066e","slc_d4cf0531e11ae8b50ac5cfff12fa28010960f4c401af25b0fa84183e34921fc7"],"source_ids":["src_3ed4e6b3352552d19bc4a4a9b495cac5"],"text":"Agent tools are organized into tool bundles, each a folder containing bin/ executables, a config.yaml, install.sh, README.md and pyproject.toml; typical tools include bash, code inspection, and editors.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0c956de854f8cbabd045791f03675d66251abc1fb1bb9055d34eda330edbe0b8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ceaade27a7a153e8190b19f540ae7f8ef223e87013115c90bbc6d54532b82caf","slc_fd9c3a0c8af003889f901d710f80567f6ad49b57dc4a07ade796c7b3214221d6"],"source_ids":["src_3ed4e6b3352552d19bc4a4a9b495cac5"],"text":"A special 'state' command runs after every action and returns a JSON string (e.g. current working directory and open file) that is parsed and used to format prompt templates.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_36192bb87d43b2124d368c59e36f7fa670d07127cbd0588414ccb0150488786b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4132655f41d079cc47c39eb3a653e2fac3ec54c11f01abf09bf9ce6070603f68"],"source_ids":["src_6b028023847e540a8896aa333212b8e4"],"text":"The EnIGMA offensive-security (CTF) mode currently recommends using SWE-agent 0.7 while EnIGMA is being updated for 1.0.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5cc5ec1d110e3874be8228c46db8d04472b0663305c8f0b3b5459b8eb58cb057","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_298879cf3ef4fc98b8c63cf24952388dc05c8e23e6846f4d39cddd552f9ff915","slc_cae97037362787843aa561e99a563716b5583e05a86f6ede51bde163362eafc2"],"source_ids":["src_5c835fd0ac895e42b487949ec61a3463"],"text":"The FAQ notes SWE-agent runs on Windows/MacOS/Linux, with the main limitation being availability of Docker containers for the environments; cloud execution is an alternative.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_609db8841c70095d682e1ac732661bf15109ed8550f693984f4ba2a5c922341c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bda7f2b7a1228d978b490886a0b44be1b2167d54652dda8b38ef6dec32702c6a"],"source_ids":["src_5c835fd0ac895e42b487949ec61a3463"],"text":"At the start of each run the agent is fed a demonstration trajectory showing how to solve an example issue, which the docs say substantially improves its ability to solve novel issues.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_691fd690eead13be218f2520a2f8cde945841369f65328d62667bf1c83d45754","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_dc0720d20a9caaf08ed4d7a6b1926cb9bab064eb3bd8b8ef6322c921f433c624"],"source_ids":["src_f89d513d9ad25ceabffd953b28a30c91"],"text":"A HistoryProcessor compresses the conversation history to make best use of the model's context window, and a parser extracts the action from the model output before it is executed in the shell session via SWEEnv.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6b6235502d377abfb7244e922251b87dd7379f7f136f3e694c2665c997add103","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_85872a2fe57b4537cbe76ea73092bb2c5321724595fe72185f8858a3ccf60fb8","slc_f56045dfe9f59038e718a77ffdc8d60624d9c12ae36422f256e0be259be92ad9"],"source_ids":["src_f89d513d9ad25ceabffd953b28a30c91"],"text":"The central entry point is the sweagent CLI, which initializes a SWEEnv environment wrapper (a thin wrapper around SWE-ReX since 1.0) and an Agent class whose forward() method prompts the model and executes its action.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_83ef7e99d45bee501f3512b5baaf6fbaa5dd7152c2e0d5c65acbc1eed0f9c84c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0555426572c6fc09240aa31234079e59bc6425810127dc8cbcd221eddf69e9d8","slc_84b61d8cf1ea255c16e065f28249014f97dfbf4fa019d4c9f23a44a5a61ec00d"],"source_ids":["src_6b028023847e540a8896aa333212b8e4","src_7da161cf69c45f85bc6607ef9dafe3bd"],"text":"A single YAML configuration governs the agent: it defines tools, prompts shown deterministically or conditionally during a trajectory, demonstrations, model behavior, and the agent-environment input/output interface.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_917cb9115361931b246d2da67b667ce4fc4d4d2295e85a44920a0ce2a7664b3b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a2dc0715b86250b0684131ee946dcd3ba60690200d86a840fc897fdc7ede7b4f"],"source_ids":["src_6b028023847e540a8896aa333212b8e4"],"text":"SWE-agent enables a user-chosen language model (e.g. GPT-4o or Claude Sonnet 4) to autonomously use tools to fix issues in real GitHub repositories, find cybersecurity vulnerabilities, or perform custom tasks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b16214a73cf65b452dcaea65c42921655f7e9ffbe1710bfcbb0c9d4972bb1a7c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b8df2913ce5cb7bfacbcb4296fbcd8c0d203884f144dfe47e0a855935da359b","slc_f56045dfe9f59038e718a77ffdc8d60624d9c12ae36422f256e0be259be92ad9"],"source_ids":["src_f89d513d9ad25ceabffd953b28a30c91"],"text":"SWEEnv relies on the SWE-ReX package: its Deployment starts a local Docker container or a remote container (e.g. modal or aws) and starts a shell session inside it that executes commands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b897a54d6ce116e473285b6067385118c0e817d05ac59b980e5e84cf95a051d5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ae7e69e53bc13cd6266ef1a643ee532748d562f61dd93ca39a39fe118ccd2079","slc_e406b29345c61044b96204ae28afd8400f399cc6ecc33f68d27c9dfbe26ddae4","slc_fd0c38847dd0c3967a1001530499c1c04c4db260fbacf782a1662661863c0800"],"source_ids":["src_5c835fd0ac895e42b487949ec61a3463"],"text":"The default response parser is function_calling, but users can configure agent.tools.parse_function to alternatives such as thought_action; custom tools can also be added per a tutorial.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bd553d401c0673abbf71a9748552733091a2d9957534a7ebccd7e1f6e785dc4e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_009ddb04f09eccc79403e14cf9869f3ac300887e5b525d3feeaa4f2f99e22daa","slc_7f5d0b92f5b976438a7c84549896a1faa466f8adad5fd14b43a09c594c495db7","slc_8317fd79b3f634b33116da46ba89fa2e80076a746ff067339295378516f0feb5"],"source_ids":["src_7da161cf69c45f85bc6607ef9dafe3bd"],"text":"Configurations are YAML files passed via the --config flag to commands like 'sweagent run' and 'sweagent run-batch'; multiple config files can be given and are merged in a nested way.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","created_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c657bdca80777e0df4caf25540ef69f81dbe37b2fa030cf08e41f71e1308f0ad","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"swe-agent/swe-agent@3ea751c087f3 snapshot 9b7bae7bd10c873c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_57d7901e5ca5927dc371f8fca243db27f418db8b080c3cc1c3809376a102a583"],"source_ids":["src_7da161cf69c45f85bc6607ef9dafe3bd"],"text":"Repository development practice: relative paths in config files resolve to the SWE_AGENT_CONFIG_ROOT environment variable if set, otherwise the repository root.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:16:49Z","updated_by_operation":"op_00b10fb97ac948d59798a97bfcbd2adc"}
